{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And when a soul offers a meal-offering.</b> This offering consists of fine flour, oil, and frankincense, as it is written: <b>fine flour shall be his offering, and he shall pour oil upon it and put frankincense on it.</b> The priest would take a handful from it — the fullness of his fist — and place it on the fire and burn it upon the altar, and the remainder was his, for so it is written: ״and the remainder of the meal-offering belongs to Aaron and to his sons, most holy of the fire-offerings of HaShem.״ And here it says מלא קומצו — the fullness of his fist — and in another place it says בקומצו — in his fist — meaning that he should not make a measured vessel for the taking. 'מלא קומצו' — one might think with a measuring vessel; Scripture says 'בקומצו.' One might think even with the tips of his fingers; Scripture says 'מלא קומצו.' How so? He covers his three fingers across the breadth of his palm and takes the fistful in the pan and the griddle, and wipes with his thumb from above and with his little finger from below, and this is one of the difficult labors in the Temple. Thus far. And Rashi, of blessed memory, explained that קומץ in the meaning of the Hebrew language is like the translation of חור, and חור is a Hebrew word; the Targum of (Nahum 2:13) ״וימלא טרף חוריו״ is בקומצא — 'with his handfuls.' If so, the word וקמץ is made clear: the essence of the commandment is the fistful, and that is what is within the חור — the hollow of the hand. And the word נפש ('soul') is not said regarding any offering except the meal-offering: who is it that typically volunteers a meal-offering? A poor person. The Holy One, blessed be He, says: I account it for him as though he offered his very soul. And it says here ״אשה ריח ניחוח לה׳״ — a fire-offering, a sweet savor to HaShem — just as is said of the bird-offering, so too of the animal-offering, and in all of them it is said thus. And the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded it to tell you: whether one brings much or whether one brings little, provided that his heart is directed toward Heaven."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:08.777614234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}